A||||6||1FieroGTRacingInc||Bigger Rim's  vs.  Lowering  ????||||5||
Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||11-09-2000||10:09 PM||||I'm working on my 87 SE and if lowering is the best thing OR  going with maybe 17" or 18" wheel's...???  what are the best thing's that ya'll have done to your's??   thank's for any help or link's...  Steve   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FieroGTRacingInc||11-10-2000||12:58 AM||||. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||11-10-2000||01:59 AM||||If you get bigger rims and your SE isn't lowered, you're gonna wanna lower it <B>soon</B>.  The wheel/tire combo will still be the same overall diamater as the original, but the smaller sidewall on the 17 or 18" wheels will make the wheel-well gap look <B>huge</B>.  If you're looking for the best handling you'll want to do both anyways.  I'd lower the car first, then save up some money and get some sweet rims  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||11-10-2000||07:58 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstpass2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstpass2.jpg</A>   before <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg</A>   after  the fender gap was bad with the 17s.. but MUCH better with the lowering springs!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||pollock||11-10-2000||09:54 AM||||As much as i'd like to lower my fiero, i've been through the ringer lowering my mustang.  Had hell getting the alignment.  <P>if you simply used lowering springs, do you guys have any problems with alignment on your lowered fieros?  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||11-10-2000||10:44 AM||||I've lowered 5 Fieros 2 of my own and have never had any problems.. other than over zelous mechanics driving them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> .. but thats not a real problem. the Toes and Camber are easy to set and you can drop your car 2" and still be able to set it all!  just go to a REAL performance shop not Goodyear or Firestone.. find a reputable performance alignment shop and i'm sure they'll set you up just right!||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||11-11-2000||12:01 AM||||thank's guy's for the information...   Steve||||reg||1
